  "goodToKnow": "Die Seide is silk: ein Seidentuch (silk scarf), reine Seide. The adjective is seiden (silken), and the idiom an einem seidenen Faden hängen means to hang by a thread. Krefeld was once Germany's Samt- und Seidenstadt (velvet and silk city). The term Seidenstraße (Silk Road) was coined in 1877 by the German geographer Ferdinand von Richthofen. Plural: die Seiden."
